 which never changes: it is immutable. A structure derived"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from it is current for it and its copies, and for no other graph, a conversion of it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"included."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Trees\/documentation\/Trees\/Tree\/generation","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/GraphGeneration":{"url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graphgeneration","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/GraphGeneration","kind":"symbol","title":"GraphGeneration","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"GraphGeneration","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"GraphGeneration","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A graph’s generation: which state of which graph it is. Every structural mutation (an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"insertion, a removal, re-pointing an edge) starts a new generation; reserving capacity and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"writing attached map values do not. A structure derived from a graph stores the graph’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"generation"},{"type":"text","text":" and asks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"isCurrent(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" before it relies on the graph again."}]}}}